From: plastron
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817: a charger's start is over 300 mA, and keeps the level from before the power-off

A Pixel 2 at 93% by its voltage read 64%, 38% and 30% at three starts, and
once 0% at 79%, which powered it off at the start (a player's logs on
ZyperOS 1.0.6, 2026-11-20: "lost 30% in 4 hours" off).

Its starts from POWER sample +108 to +114 mA into the battery, at every
level (79 to 95% at rest), with no cable in: the launcher read "off the
charger" at the start that read 0%. Another Pixel 2 reads -55 mA there, the
SoC's draw. That is over the 100 mA of a charger's start
(9-px2-rk817-start-soc.patch), so each start after 30 minutes or more off
kept the counter instead of making the level again from the voltage. And
the counter falls about 100 mA while the RK817 is off, which the voltage
start used to set right. Start to start, with a few minutes of play
between: 93% to 64% over 260 minutes off, 64% to 38% over 280, 38% to 30%
over 70, 37% to 0% over 640, 89 to 111 mA with the play taken out, while
the voltage at rest moved a point or two. So the drift piled up.

Now:

- A charger's start is over 300 mA into the battery, the charger's own end
  of a charge (the device tree's charge-term-current): a charger at work
  pushes more, 1.5 to 1.8 A at a start (1796 mA in the same logs), and
  under it the charge is over. Under it, the sample is the battery's, and
  the drop the device tree's 111 mOhm does not take out is 33 mV at most
  were the path's resistance twice that. Those starts all come from the
  voltage now: 93%, 93%, 93% and 79%.
- A charger's start keeps the level kept at the last update before the
  power-off (the nvram's remaining capacity, DATA0), not the counter, which
  drifted down for the 30 minutes or more off: 3 points after 30 minutes,
  35 after six hours. Rockchip's own driver keeps that level over a
  power-off too. The 1.0.5 case stays as it was: a cable's start at 1.5 A
  or more does not take the level from its sample.
- The start's line says the level kept beside the counter's ("counter 64%,
  kept 90%"), so a drift shows in the log.

A start after less than 30 minutes off keeps the counter, as before.

Named to sort after 9-px2-rk817-wear2-empty.patch in LC_ALL=C order, as
Buildroot applies them; start-soc-check fails if the order is ever wrong.
---
 drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c | 81 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 68 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
index 0563994..f9a8ec1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -1012,9 +1012,24 @@ static int rk817_rest_uv(int boot_uv, int boot_ua, int r_uohm)
  * rest, after 30 minutes or more off, finds the truth. The level seems to
  * fall by tens of points over the time off, with no charge lost (a report
  * on ZyperOS 1.0.5: 85% when turned off, 49% two hours later). So a
- * charger's start keeps the counter, as a start after a short time off
- * does. A drift in the counter is set right at the next start from rest or
- * at the next full charge.
+ * charger's start keeps the level it had before the power-off
+ * (rk817_start_level). A drift in it is set right at the next start from
+ * rest or at the next full charge.
+ *
+ * 300 mA: the charger's own end of a charge (the device tree's
+ * charge-term-current). A charger at work pushes more, 1.5 to 1.8 A at a
+ * start (1796 mA in a player's log), and under it the charge is over. It
+ * was 100 mA, and a start from POWER reads over that on some Pixel 2s with
+ * no cable in: one sampled +108 to +114 mA at every start from POWER,
+ * whatever its level (79 to 95% at rest), with the launcher seeing no cable,
+ * where another reads -55 mA (the SoC's draw). Each of its starts after 30
+ * minutes or more off was then a charger's start, and kept the counter,
+ * which falls about 100 mA while the RK817 is off (rk817_start_from): its
+ * battery, at 93% at rest each time, read 64%, 38% and 30% at three starts,
+ * and once 0%, which powered it off at the start (a player's logs, ZyperOS
+ * 1.0.6, 2026-11-20). Under 300 mA the sample is the battery's, and the
+ * drop the device tree's resistance does not take out is small: 33 mV at
+ * most were the path's resistance twice the device tree's.
  *
  * The rule is only for current into the battery. A start from POWER takes
  * its sample while the SoC begins to draw current, and the resistance
@@ -1022,13 +1037,13 @@ static int rk817_rest_uv(int boot_uv, int boot_ua, int r_uohm)
  * from making the level again from the voltage. Besides a full charge, that
  * is the only correction the counter gets.
  */
-#define RK817_START_CHARGING_UA	100000
+#define RK817_START_CHARGING_UA	300000
 
 /* Where a start's level comes from */
 enum rk817_start_from {
 	RK817_START_VOLTAGE,	/* off 30 min or more: the sample, at rest */
 	RK817_START_COUNTER,	/* off less: the counter, kept */
-	RK817_START_CHARGER,	/* a charger's start: the counter, kept */
+	RK817_START_CHARGER,	/* a charger's start: the level before it, kept */
 	RK817_START_NEW,	/* a battery new to the gauge: the sample */
 };
 
@@ -1036,8 +1051,12 @@ enum rk817_start_from {
  * off_min: the minutes OFF_CNT counted before this start (it counts tens of
  * minutes, and stops at 2550). After 30 minutes or more off, the level is
  * made again from the sample, as before: the driver's first author found
- * that the counter drifts down when the RK817 is off for long. A battery
- * new to the gauge has no counter to keep.
+ * that the counter drifts down when the RK817 is off for long. About 100 mA:
+ * 89 to 111 mA over 70 to 280 minutes off in a player's logs, while the
+ * battery's voltage at rest moved a point or two (as much as the sleep
+ * current the device tree gives the gauge,
+ * rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp, 100 mA). A battery new to the
+ * gauge has no counter to keep.
  */
 static enum rk817_start_from rk817_start_from(bool new_battery, int off_min,
 					      int boot_ua)
@@ -1060,6 +1079,37 @@ static enum rk817_start_from rk817_start_from(bool new_battery, int off_min,
  */
 #define RK817_LEARN_MAX_SOC	50000
 
+/*
+ * The level a start begins from, in thousandths of a percent, by where it
+ * comes from (rk817_start_from): the voltage's at rest; after a short time
+ * off, the counter (Q_PRES), which drifted down a few minutes' worth at most;
+ * and at a charger's start the level kept at the last update before the
+ * power-off (left_mah, the nvram's remaining capacity, over fcc_mah). A
+ * charger's start comes after 30 minutes or more off, and the counter has
+ * drifted down for all of it, about 100 mA: 50 mAh, 3 points, after 30
+ * minutes, and 600 mAh, 35 points, after six hours. The level kept has not,
+ * as Rockchip's own driver keeps it over a power-off. With none kept
+ * (left_mah < 0), the counter's.
+ */
+static int rk817_start_level(enum rk817_start_from from, int voltage_soc,
+			     int counter_soc, int left_mah, int fcc_mah)
+{
+	int kept;
+
+	switch (from) {
+	case RK817_START_VOLTAGE:
+	case RK817_START_NEW:
+		return voltage_soc;
+	case RK817_START_CHARGER:
+		if (left_mah < 0 || fcc_mah <= 0)
+			return counter_soc;
+		kept = (int)div_s64((s64)left_mah * 100000, fcc_mah);
+		return kept > 100000 ? 100000 : kept;
+	default:
+		return counter_soc;
+	}
+}
+
 /*
  * The full charge a start measures (RK817_NV_FULL), in mAh, or 0 when this
  * start cannot measure it.
@@ -1102,7 +1152,7 @@ rk817_read_or_set_full_charge_on_boot(struct rk817_charger *charger,
 	static const char *const from_text[] = {
 		[RK817_START_VOLTAGE] = "the voltage",
 		[RK817_START_COUNTER] = "the counter, off under 30 min",
-		[RK817_START_CHARGER] = "the counter, a charger's start",
+		[RK817_START_CHARGER] = "the level before the power-off, a charger's start",
 		[RK817_START_NEW] = "the voltage, a battery new to the gauge",
 	};
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = charger->rk808;
@@ -1112,7 +1162,7 @@ rk817_read_or_set_full_charge_on_boot(struct rk817_charger *charger,
 	int boot_ua, rest_uv, voltage_soc, counter_soc = -1;
 	int left_mah = -1, was_fcc, learned = 0, learns;
 	enum rk817_start_from from;
-	char counter[16] = "none", wear[96];
+	char counter[16] = "none", kept[16] = "none", wear[96];
 	bool first_boot;
 
 	/*
@@ -1209,8 +1259,8 @@ rk817_read_or_set_full_charge_on_boot(struct rk817_charger *charger,
 
 	from = rk817_start_from(first_boot, off_time * 10, boot_ua);
 	if (!first_boot)
-		charger->soc = from == RK817_START_VOLTAGE ? voltage_soc :
-							     counter_soc;
+		charger->soc = rk817_start_level(from, voltage_soc, counter_soc,
+						 left_mah, charger->fcc_mah);
 
 	/*
 	 * The full charge, measured at a start from the voltage at rest when
@@ -1250,12 +1300,17 @@ rk817_read_or_set_full_charge_on_boot(struct rk817_charger *charger,
 	if (counter_soc >= 0)
 		snprintf(counter, sizeof(counter), "%d%%",
 			 (counter_soc + 500) / 1000);
+	/* The level kept before the power-off, beside the counter's drift */
+	if (left_mah >= 0)
+		snprintf(kept, sizeof(kept), "%d%%",
+			 (rk817_start_level(RK817_START_CHARGER, 0, 0, left_mah,
+					    was_fcc) + 500) / 1000);
 	dev_info(charger->dev,
-		 "battery at start: %d%% from %s; off %d%s min, on 0x%02x, sampled %d mV at %d mA, at rest %d mV (%d%%), counter %s\n",
+		 "battery at start: %d%% from %s; off %d%s min, on 0x%02x, sampled %d mV at %d mA, at rest %d mV (%d%%), counter %s, kept %s\n",
 		 (charger->soc + 500) / 1000, from_text[from], off_time * 10,
 		 off_time >= 0xff ? "+" : "", on_source,
 		 (int)boot_voltage / 1000, boot_ua / 1000, rest_uv / 1000,
-		 (voltage_soc + 500) / 1000, counter);
+		 (voltage_soc + 500) / 1000, counter, kept);
 	/* Copied into the start's log with the line above (its "battery at start: ") */
 	dev_info(charger->dev,
 		 "battery at start: full charge %d mAh of the design's %d, was %d, measures %d; %s\n",
